  "problem": "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=1-v,\\,y=u+2.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n\nII. $det(A)=1$\n\nIII. The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving",
